  "slug": "bilayer-graphene-energy-spectrum-3476",
  "summary": "Recent preprints extend electronic-structure models to external fields, long-range interactions and exciton-phonon workflows in large-scale simulations.",
  "synthesis": "The three preprints share a computational focus on electronic states and their coupling to other degrees of freedom, rather than a single physical model. MLEH-LR, a machine-learning electronic Hamiltonian, adds long-range interactions and external fields and is applied to boron nitride ribbons. LeIFF treats valence electrons as dynamical spherical charge distributions in a compact force field for coupled nuclear and electronic dynamics at large scale. LetzElPhC, an open-source code, computes electron-phonon and exciton-phonon matrix elements from DFPT output of Quantum ESPRESSO and interfaces with Yambo. The new element across the set is the extension of electronic-structure descriptions to external fields, long-range terms and phonon-coupled exciton workflows, implemented through learned or reduced models and efficient codes.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
